After reviewing the file’s content, we determined the sheer number of logs makes manual checking impractical, so we’ll use the grep command to search for potential clues.

4. We will first attempt to find the flag by using the grep command to search for the known starting string, picoCTF, within the server.log file.

grep “picoCTF” server.log

The current search reveals the first part of the flag. To find the remaining parts, we will now change our search query from “picoCTF” to the log identifier “INFO FLAGPART”.

grep “FLAGPART” server.log
